getLibraryInfo [SimTalk]
Returns if the folder designated by <Folder-Path> is a library (true) or not (false).
Remarks
If the folder is a library, Plant Simulation assigns the library information to the local variables of data type
string, which you specify.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Folder-Path>.getLibraryInfo([byref Name:string, byref Version:string, 
byref Description:string, byref FilePathToLibrary:string, byRef 
IsProhibited:boolean, byRef AlternativePaths:string]) → boolean
Parameters
You can call the library with one up to seven optional parameters.
• The optional local variable Name of data type string to which the value is assigned, designates the name
of the library.
• The optional local variable Version of data type string to which the value is assigned, designates the
version of the library.
• The optional local variable Description of data type string to which the value is assigned, designates the
description of the library.
• The optional local variable FilePathToLibrary of data type string to which the value is assigned,
designates the file path of the library file (.pslib). This is useful when you want to load data from a
file, which is located in the same directory as the .pslib file.
• The optional local variable IsProhibited of data type boolean to which the value is assigned, designates if
the methods of the library do not have access to the computer (true) or do have access to the computer
(false).
• The optional local variable AlternativePaths of data type string to which the value is assigned,
designates the alternative paths of the library. If more than one path exists, the paths are separated
by a line break (strAscii(10)).
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
getLibraryInfo [SimTalk]
9-1184 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Example
.Tools.MyLibrary.getLibraryInfo(MyLibraryName, MyLibraryVersion)
