Console
The Console shows information about actions, which Plant Simulation executes.
Remarks
You can select which information the Console window shows under File > Preferences > User Interface >
Console Filter.
To record messages, display the Console by clicking 
  on the Window ribbon tab. To not record
messages, hide it.
To close the Console window, click the X in the title bar of the window. To show it again, click 
  on the
Window ribbon tab.
To auto hide the Console, click 
 . When you then click in another window, Plant Simulation hides the
window until you move the mouse over the name of the window again. To deactivate Auto Hide, click 
 .
The context menu of the Console window provides these commands:
• To copy the contents of the Console window, select the text it contains and then select Copy.
• To delete the contents of the Console window, select Clear.
• To select the entire text in the Console window, select Select All.
• Show Print Output
To show output from print commands in Methods, select this command.
• Show Info Output
To show text, which is displayed in info boxes, such as those shown during the reset and init phases
of the model, select this command. In addition, it includes warnings, for example when you use a
Console
